course: dictionary
lesson: 4736
title: Horny: hard like horn
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Horny comes from horn, the hard, tough stuff that grows on some animals. So when a text calls something horny, it usually means it is hard, rough and tough like horn. «A platypus chews its food with hard horny pads.» The word hard is a clue: the pads are not soft.
explain: Look at the words around horny to check. In «The turtle has a horny beak», a beak is the hard mouth part of a bird or turtle, so horny tells you what that beak feels like. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then try hard or tough in place of horny and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Some grown-up slang uses horny in a rude way. That meaning is not for school, so if you ever see it, ask a grown-up. In a science or nature text, horny almost always means hard like horn.
fact: Horny means hard, rough and tough, like horn.
fact: «Horny» can describe skin, beaks, pads, scales or plates.
fact: «A platypus» uses «hard horny pads» to chew its food, because adults have no teeth.
fact: Reptiles can have «horny plates» on their skin, and turtles have «a horny beak».
fact: The rude, grown-up meaning of horny is not for school; ask a grown-up if you are unsure.
exercise: «The turtle has a hard, horny beak.» What does horny mean? | Long and thin, like a worm | Soft and wet, like a sponge | Very happy and noisy | *Hard and rough, like horn
exercise: «The platypus chews its food with hard horny pads.» Find and copy one word that tells you the pads are not soft. | platypus | chews | food | *hard
exercise: «Adult platypuses have no teeth, so they chew with horny pads.» Why do they need horny pads? | Because they need horns to fight | Because they like the colour | *Because they have no teeth to chew with | Because horny pads are pretty to look at
test: The turtle's beak felt hard, rough and tough, just like horn. Which word fits? | ticklish | fluffy | *horny | watery
test: «Reptiles have horny plates on their skin.» What do the plates feel like? | Bright and shiny | Warm and wet | *Hard and tough | Soft and squishy
exam: «A platypus stuffs food into its cheek pouches, then chews it with horny pads.» What does horny mean here? | Very quick and fast | Covered in soft feathers | Glowing in the dark | *Hard and tough, like horn
